  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 232 PM EDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nNo major changes in the extended forecast. Continued summertime \ndiurnally driven convective pattern with triple digit heat index \nvalues through the next 7 days. Conditions are expected to flirt \nwith heat advisory criteria through the week, especially across east \ncentral portions of the state.\n\nFortunately, thunderstorms will be expected each afternoon which may \nhelp ease temperatures during peak heating. There is pretty good \nagreement that afternoon convection will form everyday for the \nforeseeable future, though no strong signal for severe weather \nexists with the limited shear in place. Strength of storms will \nultimately depend on heating.",
